// A name that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for env
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host reads): getenv() reads the name only up
// to the NUL, so the call would return another variable's value. A consumer
// that passes the String through prints that value, or nil, and exits 0.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string env
print "before";
print env("LOXPP_PROBE_NUL" + chr(0) + "TAIL");
